      "name": "d3d12_xs.dll",
      "group": "Graphics and memory",
      "status": "partial",
      "provider": "TuxBox Rust device and command providers with desktop D3D12 root-signature serialization.",
      "scope": "Two Xbox device profiles, eight feature queries, GPU heaps, guest-backed textures, queues, indirect compute, direct and indirect mesh dispatch, descriptor and query operations, and 32 identifiers. Frosty creates 680-byte mesh pipelines and 712-byte graphics pipelines through ID3D12Device2 and presents 3840 \u00d7 2160 frames. A fresh Proton prefix running the checkout-built providers displays the menu and video preview, opens Settings and enters the Wake Up sequence. GPU tests cover indexed draws, depth/stencil writes, NV12 plane copies, and whole and regional copies into a tiled RGBA8 texture with guest-memory writeback and alias readback. The framebuffer-preservation size getter matches the supplied DLL in its initial state. The Series VM configuration computes a process GPU address range for zero-preservation requests. Placed-texture GPU readbacks exercise that range, explicit CPU cache flush and memory profiling. Two private UMD operations implement record updates and final-release callbacks. The first three PIX callbacks support capture-device setup.",
      "remaining": "Custom firmware installation through XVIO remains unsupported. PIX requests above 32 bytes and active capture, private descriptor heaps (selector 2), nonzero framebuffer backing and profiling and cache visibility for other graphics mappings remain open. Further work includes Xbox interface methods, retail shaders, render-target and UAV writes to guest-backed textures, and overlapping writes through distinct layouts.",
